      "section": "Renewable Energy",
      "title": "Wood as an Energy Source",
      "summary": "Wood and other biomass can be used for heating and combined heat and power. Wood fuel is available as logs, chips, and pellets. Centralised, automatically fed boilers offer emissions-control advantages; chip and pellet systems feed fuel from an adjacent room or container. Pellet storage and boiler installations are comparable in space and technology to oil-heating systems. Buffer cylinders extend burning time, and a wood-fired boiler can be combined with thermal solar energy.",
