      "section": "Renewable Energy",
      "title": "Biogas",
      "summary": "Farm-scale biogas can be produced from slurry or harvested materials. Biomass is gasified in a digester and the resulting gas feeds an engine for combined heat and power. Digested slurry can be used as fertiliser and residual sludge as compost. The continuous, sensitive process requires monitoring, and a biogas plant requires a permit under the Federal Emissions Control Law. Landfill gas can also be collected and used for heat and power or heating.",
